<SiteLayout title="About" description="Why Pranam Bihar exists and how we tell Bihar’s stories." eyebrow="Why Pranam Bihar" heading="A new way to see Bihar." intro="An independent editorial home for the people, places, knowledge and living culture that make Bihar extraordinary.">
  <section class="collection"><div class="wrap prose"><p>Bihar is often spoken about through a narrow set of headlines. But no place with this much history, talent and cultural depth can fit inside a stereotype. Pranam Bihar begins with a simple belief: better stories can widen what people imagine about a place—and what a place imagines for itself.</p><h2>Curiosity before cliché.</h2><p>We want to document Bihar with care: its ancient centres of knowledge, its folk and classical traditions, its food, languages, landscapes and the everyday work of its people. We will be proud without becoming uncritical, and historical without treating Bihar as a museum.</p><h2>Built to grow.</h2><p>This website is organised as a living publication. Stories will deepen into collections, places into practical guides, and short profiles into an archive of remarkable Biharis—past and present.</p><div class="note"><blockquote>“To tell better stories about a place is to imagine a better future for it.”</blockquote></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
